I continued down the narrow street.
I stopped in front of a very old house.
An older couple was out in the spring sun.
The man stood in his garden.
He painted his house with a large brush.
The new color was light yellow.
His wife sat on a wooden bench nearby.
She relaxed and drank her warm tea.
The man saw me and paused for a moment.
He waved kindly with his brush.
"Good morning!" he said to me.
"Your house is looking really beautiful," I said.
His wife smiled at me from her bench.
"Thank you, we are enjoying the spring," she answered.
The man calmly kept painting his house.
The birds sang in their garden.
I happily continued my walk.
